f('P-01','Financial data visible to the accountant only; every read audited.','Salary profiles, adjustments, expenses, suggestions, payroll runs, payslips and finance reports are served to the accountant (and, for runs, to the configured approver). Every other role gets 403 on every finance operation. Each read is recorded in the audit log as a value-free “read” entry; exports are recorded as “export”. The audit log was checked for salary values: none.','Pass','h18 (110) and h19 (113).','Backend enforcement, encryption at rest and MFA for the accountant on the real identity server are not testable here.','Security test on the real backend.')
f('P-02','Payroll workflow rules.','One run per period; draft → approval → close; stale runs cannot be sent for approval; the approver must hold the configured role and cannot be the preparer; approval fixes the period’s entries and locks the period; close publishes payslips with notifications that carry no amounts; returned runs stay draft.','Pass','h19.','Calculation formulas (gross = base + allowances; net = gross + additions − deductions; daily rate for suggestions = base ÷ 30) and the default currency IQD are assumptions of the mock.','Owner approval of the formulas and currency.')
f('P-03','Store and custody rules.','Stock moves only on delivery; consumables never create custody; costs are entered on receipt, never returned and become a purchase expense for the accountant; counts change neither custody nor stock; the store officer has no Request_Approve call.','Pass','h14 (167).','Real stock concurrency and costing are backend concerns.','Integration tests.')
f('P-04','Contracts, warnings and appreciation letters.','Two documented steps for contract renewal; the employee never sees the recommendation; warnings follow recommendation → notice → response → decision → objection; executive sees only objected warnings; managers see only effective warnings of their team; letters are issued by the executive only and acknowledged once.','Pass','h15 (74), h16 (151), h17 (62).','The 5-working-day objection windows are shown in the dialogs but not enforced (the contract defines no error code).','Add the error code to the contract or enforce server-side.')
f('P-05','Evaluation and circulars.','Evaluation cycle, verbal grades, isolated internal notes, objection decisions, monthly department reports that freeze circular, custody and evaluation figures; circular recipients fixed at sending with one acknowledgement each.','Pass','h12 (191), h13 (72).','HR cannot adjust a grade through the contract (the decision operation has no score field).','Contract decision.')
f('P-06','Contract gaps discovered while building release 2 and 3.','(1) The executive director can send circulars but has no sent list or receipts. (2) A returned payroll run keeps its reason but the accountant has no field, notification or operation to read it. (3) Payslip operations are restricted to the employee role although managers and others need them. (4) Evaluation decision has no score field. (5) No error codes exist for the 5-working-day objection windows. (6) Salary-suggestion amounts need an owner-approved formula. (7) Default currency and hosting country are undecided.','Partial','Notes in the module reports and UNRESOLVED_ISSUES.md.','Behaviour was implemented to the contract; the requirements and the contract disagree or are silent here.','Owner/backend decision, then contract update.')
L=['# UI_AUDIT_REPORT.md','','# Nexus HR final UI/UX quality audit','','Artifact: https://claude.ai/artifact/Lq1DkrBnkkD9RiojumasKA. First audit: 5 Nov 2026 (release 1). Updated: 6 Nov 2026 after release 2 (store and custody, evaluation, circulars) and release 3 (contracts, warnings, appreciation letters, accounting) were built. GPS attendance (release “later”) is intentionally not built.','','## 1. What was actually run, and what was not','','**Executed in this audit (real runs):**','','- Static analysis of the final artifact source: operation wiring against all 307 contract operations, accessibility lint, CSS/RTL/theme lint, template-hole and markup-balance checks.',f'- {len(SUITES)} logic harnesses (Node, state-machine level, no rendering): {NCHK:,} checks, all passing ({SUITE_TXT}).',f'- Schema validation of the mock traffic those harnesses produced: {VCALLS:,} successful calls over {VOPS} operations, {VBAD} violations in {VCHK:,} checked requests and responses (545 of 1,291 calls had violations before the first audit fixes).','- Contrast ratios computed from the token values; Arabic/English key parity computed from the string tables; token values compared with the design-system specification.','','**Not run (no browser, screen reader or real backend was available):** visual rendering in any theme or direction, comparison with the light/dark reference images, responsive layouts, animation playback, keyboard and screen-reader walk-throughs, real API calls, real file upload or download. Items that depend on these are marked **Not Tested**, never Pass.','','## 2. Status and layer definitions','','- **Pass**: implemented and verified by an executed check (static or logic harness).','- **Partial**: implemented with a documented gap.','- **Fail**: expected, release-1 scope, and absent or wrong.','- **Not Tested**: not built (later release) or dependent on checks that could not be run.','- **Fully implemented UI**: the screen and its interactions are coded.','- **Interactive mock behavior**: server rules simulated in the in-page adapter (state persists across users).','- **Real API integration**: none.','','## 3. Headline numbers','','| Measure | Result |','|---|---|',f"| Contract operations wired in the UI | {len(W)} of 307 (release 1: {len(r1w)} of 175, release 2: {len(r2w)} of 56, release 3: {len(r3w)} of 70; GPS later: 0 of 6) |",f"| Release-1 operations not built | {len(r1none)} |",f"| Screens (132) | Pass {tot['Pass']} · Partial {tot['Partial']} · Fail {tot['Fail']} · Not Tested {tot['Not Tested']} |",f"| Requirement units (596, section-level) | Pass {uc['Pass']} · Partial {uc['Partial']} · Fail {uc['Fail']} · Not Tested {uc['Not Tested']} |",f"| User flows (27) | Pass {fc['Pass']} · Partial {fc['Partial']} · Fail {fc['Fail']} · Not Tested {fc['Not Tested']} |",f'| Mock vs contract schemas | {VBAD} violations in {VCALLS:,} recorded calls ({VOPS} operations) |',f'| Logic checks | {NCHK:,} passing in {len(SUITES)} suites |','','## 4. Fixes applied during this audit','','| # | Problem found | Evidence | Fix |','|---|---|---|---|','| 1 | Mock ids were not valid UUIDs after id 99 (13-digit last group) | Schema validation: 161+ violations | Last group padded to 12 digits |','| 2 | ApplicationConfiguration_Get lacked localization, auth, setting | Validation | Added the required objects |','| 3 | Attendance list responses lacked the required period summary | Validation | Summary computed from the days |','| 4 | Light-theme accent text 3.02:1, light success 3.77:1, dark error 3.89:1 | Contrast calculation | New text tokens; 30 text uses switched |','| 5 | Template form controls had no accessible name (8 controls) and no aria-invalid | Lint | aria-label and aria-invalid added |','| 6 | Table headers lacked scope | Lint (8) | scope=col |','| 7 | Escape did not close dialogs/overlays | Source search | Key handler on dialogs and showcase overlays |','| 8 | lang attribute fixed to Arabic while UI switched to English | Source | lang follows the language |','| 9 | Top-bar search did nothing | Source | Wired to Employees search for roles that can open it; hidden otherwise |','| 10 | Notification bell showed a fixed badge “4” | Source | Badge removed; sample list labelled |','| 11 | Dead “new employee” modal markup left in the template | Source | Removed |','| 12 | Assign employees to a manager (S-EMP-06) had no UI although the mock supported it | Wiring analysis | Dialog on a department manager’s file; tested |','| 13 | Payroll KPI/card shown to every role | Review against the finance-role rule | Shown only to HR, executive, accountant |','| 14 | Dashboard employee and pending-leave KPIs contradicted module data | Review | Read the shared mock |','| 15 | No skip link; main navigation unlabelled; tabs/nav lacked current state | Lint | Skip link, nav label, aria-current |','| 16 | Spinner border hard-coded white | CSS lint | currentColor |','| 17 | Reports and reviewer dashboard missing (12 operations) | Wiring analysis | Module built after the audit (h10, 135 checks) |','| 18 | Notifications missing; bell was a fake sample | Wiring analysis | Real notifications, device-token registration, bell and page (h11) |','| 19 | Reminder settings and settings hub sections missing | Wiring analysis | Reminders screen; hub driven by SystemSettings_ListSections (h11) |','| 20 | Audit log missing | Wiring analysis | Audit log screen with append-only, value-free entries (h11) |','| 21 | Evaluation draft-note id and store item ids were not valid UUIDs | Schema validation during release 2 | Ids made hexadecimal |','| 22 | Employee phone number, date of birth and address dropped by the mock on create/update | Coverage harness h20 | Stored and returned |','| 23 | 21 UI-wired operations had never been called by any harness | Validator coverage list | New harness h20 (34 checks); all now schema-validated |','| 24 | The old “Payroll” placeholder page collided with the new payslip page | Nav review | The page key is reused for payslips; label changed to “Payslip” |','| 25 | Audit log recorded no financial reads | Requirement 5.16 (every financial read audited) | Value-free “read” and “export” entries for all finance operations |','| 26 | Audit page counted operation ids inside role tables as wiring | Static analysis | Role maps and route cases are excluded from the wiring scan |','','## 5. Findings by audit category','','Columns: Identifier · Expected behavior · Implemented behavior · Status · Evidence · Issue · Required fix. Full per-requirement, per-screen and per-operation tables are in the three COVERAGE_MATRIX files.','','| Identifier | Expected behavior | Implemented behavior | Status | Evidence | Issue | Required fix |','|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|']
